1          /*******************************************************************************
2          program name: all2_vars_mi.sas
3          Title: Transgenerational, personal, and social determinants of overweight and obesity during childhood and
3        ! adolescence
4          Programmer: Yiqing Wang (nhywa)
5          			Bethsaida Cardona (n2bca) added additional variables needed for exposure windows
6          Template: Klodian Dhana /udd/nhkld/guts/proj2/imputed/5mi/program/  Jie Chen /proj/nhairs/nhair2q/progs/env_htn/
7          Preparation date: 12/2024
8          1) Purpose: Combine GUTS1 with NHS2 and conduct multiple imputation
9          2) Study Population:
10         				- NHSII 1995-2013 (for maternal exposures)
11                         - GUTS1 1996-2005 (all offsprings were >=18 by then)
12                         - GUTS2 2004-2013 (all offsprings were >=18 by then)
13         3) Inclusion:
14         	-participants who had exposure and outcome data
15            Exclusion:
16         	-Being obese or having missing BMI at the baseline for personal factors
17         	-BMI measurements excluded if pregnancy/breastfeeding during the past year
18         4) Exposures:
19         	- Maternal obesity, diet quality, physical activity, smoking, drinking, age at birth, Gestational diabetes,
19       ! C-section, Small or large for gestational age
20         	- Offspring diet quality, physical activity, sedentary behavior, Smoking, Drinking, Abnormal sleep duration
21             - Maternal education, Maternal job stress (job strain, rotating night-shift work schedule, job insecurity),
21       ! Neighborhood socioeconomic status,
22         		Number of primary care providers in the county, Food deserts/swamps, Greenspace, Air pollution (personal
22       ! exposure), Summer and winter temperature
23         	- Child abuse (both for the moms and children)
24         	- Yale food addiction scale (NHS2 and later in GUTS)
2                                                      The SAS System                         12:59 Monday, September 1, 2025

25         5) Covariates:
26         	- Maternal age at baseline (years), race/ethnicity, maternal total energy intake, maternal chronic diseases (?)
27         	- Offspring age, sex, race/ethnicity, offspring energy intake (?), offspring other chronic diseases (?)
28         6) Statistical analyses: multivariable log-binomial regression models with generalized estimating equations and
28       ! specified an exchangeable correlation structure
29         *******************************************************************************/
